{"seq":14,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:57:09.850Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"90411bd7b9baca16a563d11138e7016c7a89f16d49fc0c958e7793052cfc78d6","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two ticket numbers on Quarrendon Freight Lines in Moss's notes. Both are in shared team files you can open yourself.\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025, `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md`). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in by tablet for the 04:00 shift at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18) weren't getting their bay assignments by text. Support patched the text-message routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through the gate without anyone stepping in. The note also says to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated, `teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md`). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other North notes on Quarrendon don't have ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest covers Thea's follow-up on appointment time vs. gate arrival, and the 23 Mar 2026 note covers the renewal check-in. The 2 Jan 2026 Central handoffs note lists #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those belong to Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is a different company and isn't one of Moss's notes.\n\nI only looked at Moss's files, not Slack channels like #inc-qfl-sev1, so any ticket numbers posted there aren't on this list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
